  "observed_rules": [
    "AssignTemplate performs BeginUpdate, function metadata assignment, whole default group assignment, EndUpdate. Group.Assign includes JP/SR/LP/LR/VC/VT references.",
    "GetMicroFunctionGroupDefault returns the first registered group when nonempty except macro function48 uses factory group105; empty groups return null.",
    "ItemAndGroupByMicroFunctions0xc97ff8 searches templates in registration order and each template group in order; first JP/SR/LP/LR type match wins, with optional nonzero source-type filter.",
    "RefreshFromMicroFunctions also has six-stage VC/VT matching, detects family4 scene usage, reconciles matched template/group, and on no match chooses template58 for scene family or26 otherwise plus group56.",
    "ReconcileTemplateAndGroup reads byte flags+0x8c/+0x8d/+0x8e and remaps template/group identities; flags cannot be assumed from the selected raw byte alone.",
    "Aux UpdateMicrofunctionCodes visits all four retained source stage members+0xb0/+0xb4/+0xb8/+0xbc and encodes with retained scene/ramp/preset selectors.",
    "If Aux stage2 raw member+0xb8 is zero, microfunction types2/4/5 first seed0x19/0x11/0x17 respectively before encoding0xd5084f..0xd508c9.",
    "Every SetMicroFunctionCodeByKeyPressStage invokes virtual+0xa0 scene synchronization after updating its member.",
    "RefreshTemplateFromMacroFunction locks template callback+0xa4 while setting the recognized template. The template-after-change timer default precedes the lock check, so lock does not by itself suppress function6 block timer/expiry defaults.",
    "UpdateMicroFunction retains the old selected stage code, sets its model microfunction, refreshes macro/template, checks availability, writes encoded stage code twice around scene-index adaptation, and can convert custom template26 with scene stages to template58.",
    "SetAuxValues serializes four retained stage members for each Aux except template16 forces all four stored stage values to zero. Aux2 is serialized only when its collection count exceeds one.",
    "Refresh reads both Aux grids when present; RefreshOtherTabs delegates to parent RefreshTabs. These callbacks are not a closed isolated dialog lifecycle."
  ],
